  "body": "**Status: construction (local, verified), plus exact packing ceilings and model prices. No \u03ba claim.** This is not an admitted supplier, and the selected record is unchanged.\n\n## What is new\n\nEvery open record on the T74 borrow line uses only **high** borrowed-helper aliases from #2226. That includes #2269, #2281, #2288, #2302, #2309, #2312 and #2322; #2260 does the same on T8. None uses #2226's 32 **low (anticipatory)** aliases.\n\nThis PR builds those 32 low aliases, with their 64 initial compensation terms, on both record T74 pivot-566+554 words of #2269 (head `b479fc55`). It also builds the 5 high aliases #2269 omitted. Their T8 lenders are blocked on T74 by a paid 5\u21924 drop. An exhaustive search found rank-zero lenders among the retired X fields 12, 6, 31, 4 and 1.\n\n| word | aliases | helpers | local paid profile | local mass |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| gauge44, #2269 | 43 | 437 | `{1:2351,2:501,3:414,4:129,5:42,8:8}` | 5385 |\n| **gauge44, this PR** | **80** | **400** | `{1:2303,2:527,3:386,4:125,5:37,8:8}` | **5264** |\n| extra, #2269 | 43 | 437 | `{1:2339,2:509,3:418,4:125,5:42,8:8}` | 5385 |\n| **extra, this PR** | **80** | **400** | `{1:2287,2:535,3:386,4:125,5:37,8:8}` | **5264** |\n\nThat is \u2212121 rank units per call: \u221296 from the low aliases and \u221225 from the 5 highs. Cleanup needs 44 private zero buffers, against 76 before.\n\nThe other 16 low helpers (blocks 632, 640, 648 and 656) are **lender-blocked**. At every handoff, exactly the 32 #2226 low lenders qualify, and every low alias saves the same 3 units.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Build (`build_ext.py --controls`).** It uses #2226's replay and operators and #2269's emitter and auditor, with credit. Checks:\n- an exact free-operator replay over all 624 dirty inputs, giving Y+=X, with everything else and the buffers restored;\n- each low lender exactly equals its initial input at its handoff;\n- the 64 compensation terms equal #2226's T8 terms (only the operator ids differ);\n- dropping the compensation or flipping a sign fails;\n- the exact Gaussian handoff and exit products for all 80 warps (512 columns each);\n- #2269's `audit_local.py` passes in both orientations;\n- all 23 of its `borrow_controls` mutations are rejected.\n\n**Independent check (`check_ext.py`).** It is our own standard-library code with no PR or construction imports. It repeats the warp algebra, the anticipatory-term structure, the frame recount and the exact forward/dual replay. It has 28/28 negative controls per word. Positive controls: the canonical words and #2269's words.\n\n**Exact fixed-word packing ceiling (`cap_ext.py`).** This uses the merged `research/complex-local-word-ceiling/ceiling.py`. The cap is an upper bound on b for **any** hosting or idle refill of the fixed words. With R = 48 (T74's maximum child) it rises from **0.0017179** (#2269) to **0.0017480**, which is +1.75%.\n\n#2269 realizes 98.74% of its own cap, and #2322 reports 98.66%. At the same fraction, the new words give b \u2248 0.0017259. That is an estimate, not a claim. It is \u2248 +1.7% over the top open claim, #2322 (0.001697060).\n\n**Model prices (`price_ext.py`, idle refill modelled, not built).**\n\n| model | b | vs #2269 |\n|---|---|---|\n| favourable | 0.0017255 | +1.73% |\n| calibrated on #2269's realized refill | 0.0017127 | +0.97% |\n| calibrated on T8 | 0.0017141 | +1.05% |\n| pessimistic | 0.0016871 | \u22120.54% |\n\nThe calibrated rules overshoot their out-of-sample controls by about 2\u00b710\u207b\u2076.\n\n## What is NOT done (needed before any \u03ba)\n\n1. **Native lowering in both orientations.** This means the 64 frame-zero compensation reads, the reflected handoffs with exact Gaussian phases, and the X-register lenders. No PR has natively lowered anticipatory compensation yet.\n2. **Owner fill.** A window-exact owner fill at 400 helpers per call is needed, including ownership of X fields 1, 4, 6, 12, 31 and 73, and owner lifetimes covering the 32 start-of-call reads.\n3. **Charges.** The 44 buffers and the 64 terms still need charges.\n4. **The rest of the pipeline.** PLAN/SPEC refreeze, the certified price, and the outer assembly (#1673 et al.) remain.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/t74-low-alias-borrowing/run_all.py --fetch\npython3 -I -B research/t74-low-alias-borrowing/cap_ext.py\n```\n\nThis takes about 25 s with the standard library. The expected last lines begin with `PASS_T74_LOW_ALIAS_RUN_ALL check=PASS price=PASS crosscheck=PASS` and `PASS_T74_LOW_ALIAS_PACKING_CAPS cap48_high43=0.001717935929 cap48_ext80=0.001747958372`.\n\nThe rebuild needs numpy: `run_all.py --build --numpy-site DIR`. It reproduces `words/` and `witness/` byte for byte.\n\nChecks run locally:\n- the package metadata check passes;\n- the 65 `test_research_*` tests pass;\n- the scripts parse under the 3.10 grammar;\n- the registered Python 3.12 replay was **not** run (it is not installed).\n\n## Provenance and credit\n\n- **Base:** `0fdd7d82` (priority revision 4), unchanged at submission.\n- **Track and claim:** 20\u201339 (complex supplier), OS seed 35. Card: `complex-new-helper-inventory`, refined. No sprint coordination issue exists, so the claim was recorded locally.\n- **Predecessors:**\n  - Cinna Davis / 1337isnot1337 (#2226): the mechanism, the 80-alias witness, replay and operators.\n  - Jeremy Kothe (#2269): T74 words, the 43-alias witnesses, the emitter, auditor and controls (vendored).\n  - Dugongue (#2260): high aliases on T8.\n  - Vlado Vojdanovski (#2322): found independently and concurrently that retired source fields can be rank-zero lenders for high roles. Our 5 extra high lenders use the same idea.\n  - Douglas Colkitt et al.: the merged ceiling tool.\n- **Related:** our own independent check of #2269 is #2315.\n\nPrepared for Sagar Thakrar with substantial AI assistance (Claude Code, Anthropic): one subagent built the construction, others wrote the independent checker and pricing harness, and another reviewed it adversarially. The main session reran the checks and computed the caps. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
